          "content": [
            {
              "type": "reasoning",
              "text": "The 细笔画初稿 (R4): the gap appears on the right side. Looking at the image: it's a \"C\" shape with gap on the right. The upper arc ends at around upper-right (approx 45°?), and the lower arc ends at lower-right. So the gap opens to the right (右侧), slightly... The gap seems centered toward the right, maybe slightly right-of-center. Let me examine more carefully — the top end appears at ~30-40° above horizontal on the right, and bottom end at ~30-40° below horizontal. So gap faces right (正右方), roughly centered on the right/slightly lower? Actually the gap looks like it spans from upper-right to lower-right, centered on the right side.\n\nAnswer: gap faces right (3 o'clock direction). Note that this is the same as current version (R43)? Current also appears gap on the right. But the question is just about R4.\n\nLet me be careful — maybe the gap is slightly toward the upper-right in R4. Let me zoom mentally: The image shows the stroke ending at top around x=145,y=62 (upper right) and at bottom around x=135,y=130. The gap center is roughly right and slightly lower... Hmm. I'll say it opens to the right side (roughly at 3 o'clock, with opening spanning upper-right to lower-right).\n\nI could verify by reading image again? Not needed. Provide answer."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**R4「潮位标记 · 细笔画初稿」：缺口朝右（约 3 点钟方向）**，也就是朝右开放，口子从右上斜向一直撑到右下斜向，两条笔画端点都收在右半边；整体就是一个开口朝右的细笔画 “C”。\n\n对照现在看的 R43 当前稿，缺口同样在右侧，只是笔画明显加粗了。"
            }
          ],
